From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 4 Aug 2026 15:03:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] fix(preview): recover the frame when an OAuth redirect
 navigates it off the app
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

This lands the OAuth-escape work that had been sitting uncommitted in the
working tree, and completes the half of it that was missing.

The problem it solves: a "Sign in with Google" button inside a previewed app is
a full-page navigation to a third-party origin. The iframe dutifully follows,
the provider's login page renders inside the preview pane, and there is no way
back — the address bar belongs to the app, not the frame, and the provider will
never redirect somewhere our sandbox serves.

Detection is a liveness handshake. The parent pings the frame on every load;
our injected bridge answers. On a third-party origin the bridge does not exist,
so the silence IS the signal, and the parent restores the preview to "/". A
2.5s debounce keeps a genuine escape from looping, and the check only arms
after the bridge has answered at least once, so a cold first load is never
mistaken for an escape.

The uncommitted version had only the parent half. Nothing answered
lifemark-preview-ping and nothing sent origin/href with location messages, so
the origin check was inert and — worse — every subsequent full-page load in a
frame whose bridge had once been alive got no pong and bounced the user back to
"/". So veb-bridge.ts now implements the guest side, which is what makes the
feature real rather than a false-positive generator. Existing sandboxes pick it
up on their next file sync, since the injected script's content changes.

Also from that work: normalizeSandboxPathname now hardens the address-bar sync
against absolute URLs (a pasted or redirected https://… must never become an
iframe src path segment), and isSamePreviewOrigin covers the inverse case of a
bridge still alive on a document that is no longer ours.

docker.ts keeps only the failure diagnostic from the uncommitted version — its
waitForInnerHttp is superseded by waitForLocalServer from the previous commit,
which probes inside the container on every path rather than only when the app
runs on Docker Desktop, and reads the container's real port instead of assuming
5173.

tsc --noEmit: 51 errors before, 51 after, identical per file. Build passes.
